From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:40:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] webxdc: member list and member avatars for apps

Port of chatmail/core simon/webxdc-memberlist-and-avatars (three commits,
squashed), so an app can show who is in the chat.

jsonrpc get_webxdc_memberlist(account_id, instance_msg_id) returns
(user id, display name) tuples for every chat member with a known key,
plus self. The user id is the per-app hash selfAddr already uses,
sha256("<fingerprint hex>-<instance rfc724_mid>"), so a member's id here
equals the selfAddr their own device reports, and the status updates they
send can be matched to an entry. Self is added even in 1:1 chats (which
don't list it) and after being removed from a group.

get_webxdc_blob serves a virtual directory: `__webxdc__/avatar/<user id>.jpg`
is that member's profile image, so ids stay the only handle an app gets
and contact ids never leave core.

Display names come from Contact::get_display_name_without_email (new):
the local nickname, else the contact's own name, never the address. Unlike
upstream's branch, self gets the configured display name rather than the
localized "Me", matching selfName.
